# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node / web build
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Original user-supplied data dump -- not used by the running app (server/main.py
# reads from app/data/ + app/raw_sources/ instead), and far too large for git.
data/

# server/main.py's own on-demand csv/xlsx/parquet cache (local-dev mode only --
# deliberately separate from web/public/parquet/ below, so it never collides with
# or overwrites the static site's own pre-generated files). Regenerated on first
# request; never commit.
app/on_demand_cache/

# The synced master parquet (~80 MB, from Google Drive -- see
# scripts/sync_from_drive.py), used only by server/main.py's local-dev mode.
# Never commit; each environment fetches its own copy.
app/data/

# web/public/catalog.json, web/public/parquet/, and web/public/raw_sources/ are NOT
# ignored -- they're exactly what the deployed static site ships (see
# scripts/build_catalog.py's docstring), generated on a machine with full `to JD/`
# access. Committing them is what lets GitHub Pages -- or any other static host --
# run without that tree, or a backend, at all. See README.md "Adding new data".
